id:                     E603
trigger_tool:           cmake
phase:                  linking
error_signature:        Error loading shared library .*/lib.*\.so|LoadName: <Not found>|LINK_FLAGS.*soname.*missing|build\.ninja.*soname.*missing
severity:               3
category:               ohos, cmake, linking, packaging, portability
match_keywords:         LINK_FLAGS, CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS, CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS_RELEASE, CMakeToolchain, build.ninja, SONAME, OUTPUT_NAME, cpp_info.libs
title:                  Legacy target LINK_FLAGS can vanish from Conan CMake Ninja shared-link rules
root_cause:             A source patch can set a legacy target LINK_FLAGS SONAME option and configure successfully while the generated Ninja shared-link rule omits it; under a config-specific Conan CMake build, setting only a source property or only the generic cache flag can therefore leave the ELF without DT_SONAME even though the output filename is correct
affected_scope:         Conan CMakeToolchain builds using Ninja for OHOS shared libraries where legacy target LINK_FLAGS or a single non-config-specific linker flag is expected to control SONAME or another required shared-link option
verification_cmd:       compare the patched target property with CMakeCache.txt and the exact build.ninja shared-link argv, then inspect DT_SONAME with llvm-readobj and compile a Conan consumer using the logical -l stem
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           cache-bound-shared-linker-flags
rec_description:        Inject the required shared-link option through CMakeToolchain cache_variables for both CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS and the active build-type variant such as CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS_RELEASE; verify the generated linker argv, keep OUTPUT_NAME as the logical stem without the conventional lib prefix, and expose the same stem through cpp_info.libs
rec_command:            set CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS and CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS_RELEASE in CMakeToolchain.cache_variables, run conan create, inspect build.ninja and llvm-readobj --dynamic-table, then verify the consumer links with -l<logical-stem>
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               manual
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      modern-target-link-options
fallback_description:  If recipe-wide flags would affect multiple shared targets, replace the legacy LINK_FLAGS property with target_link_options on the exact target and verify that the generated Ninja rule contains the option
fallback_command:       target_link_options(<target> PRIVATE -Wl,-soname,<name>) followed by build.ninja and ELF dynamic-table readback
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          manual
forbid_1_pattern:       set_target_properties.*LINK_FLAGS.*without.*link argv readback
forbid_1_reason:        A configured target property does not prove that the selected generator emitted the option into the active configuration's shared-link rule
forbid_1_consequence:   The build succeeds with the expected filename but consumers retain a build-tree NEEDED identity
forbid_2_pattern:       infer SONAME from output filename|set only CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS when a config-specific value overrides it
forbid_2_reason:        A shared object can have the expected filename but no DT_SONAME
forbid_2_consequence:   Consumers record a build-tree relative NEEDED path and fail on the target
principles:             P007
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E267, E330, E383, E600]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E603-draft-A7C1.md
last_updated:           2026-09-08
source_event:           liblemon 1.3.1.8 W3 run-018 proved legacy LINK_FLAGS absent from the Ninja link argv; liblemon 1.3.1 W3 run-032 passed 42/42 upstream, 3/3 state, and 1/1 consumer after generic plus RELEASE cache injection
authors:                A7C1
